in the far north of norway it is forever  winter this is exercise cold response  several weeks of military games  involving 30 000 troops from 27  countries most of them nato alliance  members  these troops are from finland a country  with a long shared border with russia  finland's not a nato country and it's  historically neutral but since the  invasion of ukraine an increasing number  of finns and neighboring swedes want  their nations to join the nato alliance  it's worrying the soldiers the civilians  and it's not nice  it's something we speak about often  and everyone in here just wants peace  not a war  but these soldiers are reluctant to  discuss what abandoning neutrality might  actually mean i think that that is a  political question and maybe  i i won't answer to that one  while a real war rages in eastern europe  these troops from finland and other  countries are being put through their  paces in the harshest of possible  climates in the hope that these skills  will never have to be used for real  theater we're showing around a  state-of-the-art field hospital that can  be erected in a matter of hours  precisely the kind of equipment  ukrainian forces desperately need but  can't get their hands on  and elsewhere this norwegian made  anti-aircraft weapon the only one in the  world  nato countries have spent billions of  dollars arming ukraine but supplies have  to be carefully calibrated  do too much and risk being drawn into a  direct conflict with russia  the invasion of ukraine poses the  biggest threat to european security in a  generation  several nato states are now rushing to  ramp up their defence spending and the  uk and norway announced a new agreement  on defending the increasingly strategic  arctic as the west weans itself off  russian energy supplies it's looking to  norway to make up for shortfalls of oil  and gas the arctic sea also has rich  fishing grounds and future trade routes  we have to be in a position to uphold  our our rules and our international laws  such as freedom navigation should the  ice melt even further and the countries  like china will seek to use maybe these  routes  to sail through and russia might seek  these routes to control these are long  planned exercises but no matter how you  frame this they're a massive show of  force aimed squarely at moscow 220  aircraft 50 warships tens of thousands  of troops putin's actions in ukraine  have rejuvenated old alliances and  expanded nato's reach and appeal  precisely the opposite of what the  kremlin wants leave barker al-jazeera in  northern norway
 

